                <pb facs="0469" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/377: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-09T12:00:00+08:00">October 9,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:47 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>873. My 854, October 3, 8 p.m. Following from American Consul at Harbin: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 8, 4 p.m. Reliably informed Soviet regulars or partisans
                            recently killed unarmed male inhabitants White Cossack villages, Three
                            Rivers district, Heilungkiang Province, reasons unknown, possibly
                            provocation to cause White indignation against the Reds.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
